;; The host-ABI conformance fixtures, as a WORKSPACE
;; (`DECISIONS.md#workspace-capabilities`).
;;
;; It exists for ONE grant: `hostreq.cljc` calls `flint.host/request`, which is
;; guarded `:host`, and a guard is satisfied by what a workspace HOLDS rather
;; than by what it asserts -- the analyzer reads `:grants` and nothing else, so
;; a fixture cannot mint the authority by claiming it.
;;
;; The name matters as much as the grant. Without this file a workspace's
;; identity falls back to the source root's PATH, which is machine-specific and
;; reads badly in a diagnostic, as `lib/deps.edn` says for the same reason.
{:flint/workspace flint/conform-host
 :flint/capabilities-grant [:host]}
